WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.925
Every other migration changes which
system answers the question, who is this?

2
00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:07.412
Certificates are how
the answer gets proved.

3
00:00:07.412 --> 00:00:10.837
And a certificate isn't a record
you move with the directory.

4
00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:15.165
It's a signed statement that's already
been handed out, sitting in devices,

5
00:00:15.165 --> 00:00:19.276
smart cards, servers and trust
stores nobody remembers configuring.

6
00:00:19.276 --> 00:00:25.250
It keeps working, unchanged, until it expires,
and then whatever relied on it stops.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:31.787
Domain controllers, Wi-Fi, VPN, server
encryption and PIV sign-in all lean on it.

8
00:00:31.787 --> 00:00:35.213
Each book in this workbook
migrates its own consumers.

9
00:00:35.213 --> 00:00:38.287
None of them owns the issuer
underneath all of them.

10
00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:41.210
That's the problem, and it
runs on a different clock.
